{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.2.b9cdfcf54c","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"pron-o-10","passage":"<p>The club announced that ______ new schedule had been approved.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["its","their","they're","it's"],"answer":"A","explanation":"A pronoun must agree with the noun it refers to. Here that noun is “the club,” which is singular. The singular possessive pronoun is “its” (“it's” means “it is”)."},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.2.bf51a227f6","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"tense-2","passage":"<p>Over the past decade, the school ______ four new clubs.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["will add","had added","has added","added"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The verb tense must fit the time frame of the sentence, which is set by “Over the past decade,” a period that continues up to the present, so the present perfect (“has” plus the past participle) is needed. The correct choice is “has added.”"},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.2.ca48cf3e33","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"tense-3","passage":"<p>In recent years, the company ______ dozens of new engineers.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["hired","had hired","will hire","has hired"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The verb tense must fit the time frame of the sentence, which is set by “In recent years,” a period that continues up to the present, so the present perfect (“has” plus the past participle) is needed. The correct choice is “has hired.”"},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.2.3db033b2ab","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"tense-10","passage":"<p>Since 2015, the bakery ______ several new pastries.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["will introduce","has introduced","had introduced","introduced"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The verb tense must fit the time frame of the sentence, which is set by “Since 2015,” a period that continues up to the present, so the present perfect (“has” plus the past participle) is needed. The correct choice is “has introduced.”"}
